// Resource depth is deliberately not a causal or CPU-capacity verdict.
const TraceSchedulerConcurrencyTeaching = "For simultaneous ready/running thread counts use window_stats.scheduler_concurrency (not a new view). Each physical source and state has its own accepted closed-interval population across positive TIDs; query_pid is context, not a filter. Same-thread intervals are unioned before a half-open sweep. peak_threads is an instantaneous count; mean_threads divides thread_ms by the full query window, not active time or nonzero buckets. busy_ms is union time; thread_ms is thread·ms, not response delay. Read coverage and omitted groups/segments: open tails and source/identity conflicts are excluded, not filled to the window end or measured as idle. Values describe confirmed intervals only, not complete capture. Keep Runnable and Running separate, and use business language such as 同时等待CPU的线程数、同时运行的线程数. Only independent on-chain evidence can establish a target root cause or priority inversion."
